          #sectiona.num_section
          %h2#introduction.num_section Introduction
          %p
            %a{:href => "#MR764972"}> Michor 1984a
            ,
            %a{:href => "#MR767683"} 1984b
            gives a description of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of “smooth manifolds” due to himself and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Kriegl"} Kriegl
            which is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed"} cartesian closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            in the finite dimensional situation. This is also true in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+space"} Banach space
            situation; which is not stated in the paper, but follows readily from the finite dimensional situation.
          #sectionb.num_section
          %h2#definition.num_section Definition
          %p The final data of a “smooth manifold” is the following:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Two sets,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T M
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi M
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi T
                      %mi M
                      %mo →
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi _{M} \colon T M \to M
                such that each fibre is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+space"} locally convex space
                of a certain type.
            %li
              %p
                A set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S} (\mathbb{R},M)
                of curves in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                = succeed "\u2013reparametrisations" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
            %li
              %p
                For each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in \mathbb{R}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi t
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta _{t} \colon \mathcal{S} (\mathbb{R},M) \to T M
                such that:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mi M
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi δ
                            %mi t
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ev
                            %mi t
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi _{M} \circ \delta _{t} = \ev_{t}
                    ,
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi δ
                            %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi f
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi δ
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta _{t} (c \circ f) = f'(t) \delta _{f(t)} c
                    ,
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                    is constant if for all
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
                    then
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi δ
                              %mi t
                            %mi c
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta _{t} c = 0
            %li
              %p
                A mapping
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Pt
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Pt
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi M
                      %mo ,
                      %mi T
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pt^{T M} = \Pt\colon \mathcal{S} (\mathbb{R},M) \times \mathbb{R} \to \mathcal{L} (T M, T M)
                such that:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Pt
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mrow
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi M
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mrow
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi M
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pt(c,t) \colon T_{c(0)} M \to T_{c(t)} M
                    is linear and continuous,
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Pt
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Id
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pt(c,0) = \Id
                    ,
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Pt
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
